      "title": "diameter: Define custom entity in a valid fashion",
      "message": "diameter: Define custom entity in a valid fashion\n\nThe suggestion of what to do in Custom.xml did not produce valid XML.\n\nThis is an actually valid XML method of having a &Custom; entity\nthat itself includes other entities. The separate file should be\na parameter entity, which then defines a custom entity into which\nthe other entities are added.\n\nThis will maintain our practice of keeping the \"dictionary.xml\"\nfile as constant and allowing people to change only the \"Custom\"\nfile and add new files.\n\nUsing \".ent\" is a more normal extension for this; might as well\nchange it as things are going to break anyway because the old\nconfiguration wouldn't work.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-08-21T21:11:15.000-04:00",
